    "body": "This PR fixes #476 .\n\n## Summary\n\nOn SM90, `deep_gemm.fp8_einsum(\"bhr,hdr->bhd\", a, b, d, c)` returns `a @ b.T` instead of `c + a @ b.T`: `c` is silently dropped.\n\n- The host first copies `c` into `d`, expecting the kernel to add `a @ b.T` onto `d` ([gemm.hpp L49\u2013L51](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/blob/1fc9c66975ee322d628b3288534ca0e9ce12a64d/csrc/apis/gemm.hpp#L49-L51)).\n- On SM90, `sm90_fp8_bmm` launches `sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d_impl`, which cannot add onto `d`. It writes `d` with a plain TMA store ([sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d.cuh L434](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/blob/1fc9c66975ee322d628b3288534ca0e9ce12a64d/deep_gemm/include/deep_gemm/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d.cuh#L434)), which overwrites `c`. `sm90_fp8_bmm` sets `with_accumulation` ([L300](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/blob/1fc9c66975ee322d628b3288534ca0e9ce12a64d/csrc/jit_kernels/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d.hpp#L300)), but never passes it to the kernel ([L36\u2013L61](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/blob/1fc9c66975ee322d628b3288534ca0e9ce12a64d/csrc/jit_kernels/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d.hpp#L36-L61)).\n- The other launcher of this kernel, `sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d`, rejects `c` ([L81](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/blob/1fc9c66975ee322d628b3288534ca0e9ce12a64d/csrc/jit_kernels/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d.hpp#L81)). `sm90_fp8_bmm` does not ([L290](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/blob/1fc9c66975ee322d628b3288534ca0e9ce12a64d/csrc/jit_kernels/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d.hpp#L290)).\n\n`\"bhr,hdr->bhd\"` is the only `fp8_einsum` expression that runs on SM90, and `tests/test_einsum.py` passes `c` to it only on SM100, which accumulates correctly. \n\nReproduction: See Issue #476 .\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd the missing `not c.has_value()` check to `sm90_fp8_bmm`, as in `sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d`. Passing `c` on SM90 now raises an error instead of returning a wrong result. As with `sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d`, `d` has already been overwritten with `c` when the error is raised.\n\n```diff\n--- a/csrc/jit_kernels/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d.hpp\n+++ b/csrc/jit_kernels/impls/sm90_fp8_gemm_1d2d.hpp\n@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@ static void sm90_fp8_bmm(const torch::Tensor& a, const torch::Tensor& sfa,\n                          const int& batch_size, const int& m, const int& n, const int& k,\n                          const cute::UMMA::Major& major_a, const cute::UMMA::Major& major_b, const cute::UMMA::Major& major_sfb,\n                          const std::string& compiled_dims) {\n-    DG_HOST_ASSERT(d.scalar_type() == torch::kBFloat16);\n+    DG_HOST_ASSERT(not c.has_value() and d.scalar_type() == torch::kBFloat16);\n     DG_HOST_ASSERT(major_a == cute::UMMA::Major::K and major_b == cute::UMMA::Major::K);\n \n     const auto desc = GemmDesc {\n```\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_fp8_bhr_hdr_bhd` already checks `c` on SM100. This PR adds the SM90 counterpart: a call with `c` must raise. The accumulator has the layout of the SM100 check (`[h, b, d]` viewed as `[b, h, d]`), in BF16, the only `d` type `sm90_fp8_bmm` accepts.\n\n```diff\n                         assert_stochastic_bf16_matches_fp32_accumulation(\n                             z_sr, launch_accumulated, f'{b=}, {h=}, {r=}, {d=}')\n+                    else:\n+                        # SM90's FP8 BMM kernel cannot add C into D, so C must be rejected\n+                        acc = torch.zeros((h, b, d), device='cuda', dtype=torch.bfloat16).permute(1, 0, 2)\n+                        try:\n+                            deep_gemm.fp8_einsum('bhr,hdr->bhd', x_fp8, y_fp8, acc, c=acc)\n+                        except RuntimeError:\n+                            pass\n+                        else:\n+                            raise AssertionError(f'{b=}, {h=}, {r=}, {d=}: C must be rejected on SM90')\n```\n\nTested on an H100 80GB HBM3 (driver 580.126.09, CUDA 13.0, torch 2.9.1+cu130), on `main` (1fc9c66) and on this branch, both built with `./develop.sh`. The test functions run in the order of `__main__`, after one warm-up `bench_kineto` call. Without the warm-up, `python tests/test_einsum.py` stops at its first benchmark with a `ZeroDivisionError` on both trees, because `bench_kineto` returns 0 on its first call in a process (#426).\n\n`main` with the new test: the call with `c` does not raise, so the test fails.\n\n```\nTesting \"bmk, bnk -> mn\":\nTesting \"bhr, hdr -> bhd\":\nTesting \"bhd, hdr -> bhr\":\nTesting \"bhd, bhr -> hdr\":\nTesting FP8 \"bhr, hdr -> bhd\":\n...\nAssertionError: b=4, h=8, r=4096, d=1024: C must be rejected on SM90\n```\n\nThis PR:\n\n```\nTesting \"bmk, bnk -> mn\":\nTesting \"bhr, hdr -> bhd\":\nTesting \"bhd, hdr -> bhr\":\nTesting \"bhd, bhr -> hdr\":\nTesting FP8 \"bhr, hdr -> bhd\":\ntest_fp8_bhd_hdr_bhr:\n > Filtered by <function <lambda> at 0x73748c055760>\ntest_fp8_bhd_bhr_hdr:\n > Filtered by <function <lambda> at 0x73748c055800>\nALL TESTS PASSED\n```\n",
